@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] core-is-plain-kotlin
`android/core` is plain Kotlin with no Android or Compose dependency, so its logic is
tested on the JVM by `:core:test`. Logic that can be pure (ranking, parsing, paths, ways
of motion) lives here and the app calls it.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] core-work-notice-real-time
The ongoing AI notification summary MUST include only running whole-diff work and MUST
use the oldest running task's server start time for elapsed time. A missing or future
start MUST omit elapsed time. Terminal tasks MUST disappear independently when other
tasks still run (Tavi's 20 Oct request to explore app notifications for ongoing AI work).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:motion;architecture] core-page-way
`pageWay` turns two places into forward or backward from their order, and `swipeStep`
turns a drag and its release speed into the next or previous page: a throw of 500dp/s
counts however short, and a throw against the drag cancels it (rule 105).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] core-file-links-from-root
Links are resolved from the repository root: `./` and `../` never go above it and a
dot-folder keeps its dot (rule 124; J36).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] core-path-cut-from-the-left
A shortened path keeps its end and drops whole folders from the front, never cutting a
name in the middle (rule 90).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] core-search-every-word
A list search matches a row when every word typed is in it, in any order (rule 101).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] core-changelog-reads-old-and-new
`parseChangelog` reads `## <version>` sections with a summary and bullets, and `###`
groups inside them; a section with groups still reads as one list of the same bullets on
a build that does not know groups (rule 127). A `![alt](changelog/<version>/<name>.png)`
line is a picture under the bullet it follows; it MUST stay unindented under a bullet so a
build from before 0.40.0 skips it instead of showing it as text (Tavi, 16 Oct 10:49).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture] core-contracts-follow-the-grammar
`parseContracts` follows the `@cc` grammar of the code-contracts skill: a directive line,
optional `[key:value,...]` metadata, an ID token and non-empty prose up to the next
directive. A malformed directive, empty prose, text before the first directive or a
repeated ID is reported as a problem, never silently dropped.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] checks-new-failures-only
The check evaluator MUST baseline the first complete known-head snapshot and deduplicate
stable occurrences across persisted restarts. Reruns MUST require timestamp or observed
state-transition evidence. Cancelled, unknown, skipped and neutral outcomes and partial
reads MUST NOT become failures. Source, authentication, generation or follow-revision
mismatch MUST reject delivery (Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, notification expansion).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] core-ai-result-alerts-require-explicit-owned-task
AI outcome alerts MUST match an explicitly persisted task ID, key and kind. Only
authoritative done or failed statuses MAY alert; cancelled settles silently, and missing,
unknown or network interruption MUST NOT imply an outcome. Expired ownership MUST NOT
produce a late alert (Tavi, 21 Oct 2026, notification expansion).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security] core-updates-confine-access-headers
Update URLs and every redirect MUST match the configured server's scheme, host and
effective port before any request is opened or Access headers attached. Automatic
redirects MUST stay disabled (repository review 15 Oct 2026, finding 7).

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;security] core-browser-repo-needs-address-evidence
Browser repository detection MUST use only visible, unfocused native address-field text
with an exact resource ID allowlisted for the foreground browser package. Page content,
links, descriptions, unknown fields and stale or conflicting evidence MUST NOT produce
a repository. An accepted address MUST name exactly github.com or www.github.com over
HTTPS (or the browser's schemeless display), contain a valid owner and repository, and
exclude GitHub's non-repository routes, credentials, ports, encoded or ambiguous text.
The result MUST retain only owner and repository, with subpages reduced to their root
(Tavi, 18 Oct 2026: the browser floaty appears only on a GitHub repository and opens that
repository in Pully; screenshot capture is excluded).
